\name{cellucid_camera_path_keyframe_add}
\alias{cellucid_camera_path_keyframe_add}
\title{Add a camera path keyframe}
\usage{
cellucid_camera_path_keyframe_add(viewer, camera, embedding, hold, label)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{camera}{The camera to save, whole (one from camera_framing or views_state); omitted, the selected view's camera now. A named list. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does). \describe{\item{\code{freefly}}{A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{pitch}}{A number. Required.}\item{\code{position}}{A vector or list of a number (at least 3 items, at most 3 items). Required.}\item{\code{yaw}}{A number. Required.}}}\item{\code{navigationMode}}{"orbit", "planar" or "free" (free-fly). One of \code{"orbit"}, \code{"planar"}, \code{"free"}. Required.}\item{\code{orbit}}{A named list. Required. \describe{\item{\code{phi}}{A number. Required.}\item{\code{radius}}{A number (more than 0). Required.}\item{\code{target}}{A vector or list of a number (at least 3 items, at most 3 items). Required.}\item{\code{targetRadius}}{A number (more than 0). Required.}\item{\code{theta}}{A number. Required.}}}}}
\item{embedding}{The embedding the keyframe was recorded on; omitted, the one the selected view shows. Either a named list (An embedding: the obsm array and the columns of it plotted); or \code{NULL}. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does). \describe{\item{\code{columns}}{The 0-based columns plotted, one per dimension. A vector or list of a whole number (at least 0) (at least 1 item, at most 3 items, each once). Required.}\item{\code{key}}{The obsm key, "X_umap". Text (at least 1 character). Required.}}}
\item{hold}{Seconds the camera rests at the keyframe before moving on; omitted, 0 (none). A number (at least 0). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{label}{The keyframe's label, the shot's name: in the Camera path list, and, while the path plays with captions on (the default), its caption over the plot from halfway into the move to it until halfway out of it, as a documentary's title ("Beta cells", "Overview"; short, a title case phrase). Omitted, "KF n", which is never captioned. Unique among the keyframes. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
