\description{
Save a camera as the next keyframe of the camera path (before the return to start, when there is one), optionally with a hold: seconds the camera rests there.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{camera-path.keyframe.add} (Camera path). It changes what the viewer shows: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{camera-path}.
}
